Description: Estimates quantile-on-quantile regression (QQR) models in the
    sense of Sim and Zhou (2015) <doi:10.1016/j.jbankfin.2015.01.013>,
    which describe how the effect of a designated regressor on the
    conditional quantiles of a response varies across the quantiles of that
    regressor. The fitting function 'qqr()' runs Gaussian-kernel weighted
    local linear quantile regressions (Yu and Jones 1998
    <doi:10.1080/01621459.1998.10474104>) at a grid of empirical quantiles
    of the regressor, with optional control variables, kernel weights on
    either the regressor scale or the empirical distribution function scale
    of Sim and Zhou, and pointwise p-values from 'quantreg'. Automatic
    bandwidth rules (Silverman, robust and IQR rules of thumb, check-loss
    cross-validation, Sheather-Jones and Ruppert-Sheather-Wand plug-ins, and
    'np' cross-validation) are stored with a reporting description. Further
    tools compare the regressor-averaged QQR surface with standard quantile
    regression, extract and export surfaces to tables, 'Excel' and 'Word',
    draw static and interactive three-dimensional surfaces, heatmaps and
    contour plots, and summarise the bivariate quantile dependence of the
    data with rank correlation, Somers' D, Blomqvist's beta and
    co-exceedance measures.
